  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "dokoro de ha nai / dokoro de ha naku\n\nDokoro dewa nai goes at the end of a sentence. Dokoro dewa naku goes in the middle.",
      "html": "dokoro de ha nai / dokoro de ha naku<br/><br/>Dokoro dewa nai goes at the end of a sentence. Dokoro dewa naku goes in the middle.",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "f2cedd0889b1a601a9b8a5c735fb3a7b4af0d4497d632c051642a6a8384315ba",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "＊Use this grammar to strongly deny something.\n\nFORMATION:\nＶ(plain form) + どころではない\nいＡ + どころではない\nなＡ・Ｎ + どころではない\n\nAs for どころではなく, this grammar fits into the middle of a sentence, as in example #6271. どころではない is meant to end a sentence.",
      "html": "＊Use this grammar to strongly deny something.<br/><br/>FORMATION:<br/>Ｖ(plain form) + どころではない<br/>いＡ + どころではない<br/>なＡ・Ｎ + どころではない<br/><br/>As for どころではなく, this grammar fits into the middle of a sentence, as in example #6271. どころではない is meant to end a sentence.",
      "credits_raw": "rubyhatchet",
      "content_sha256": "3c9b47c8ce73dcd99be28fd8e8d5fff228fa46bbc9686dbb176e2a90f1836bd7",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "ex #1160 若いどころか (far from being young )\nex #3759 彼は紳士どころではない。(He is far from being a gentleman. )\nQuestion: Is there is difference in these sentences between \"どころか\" and \"どころではない\" ?",
      "html": "ex #1160 若いどころか (far from being young )<br/>ex #3759 彼は紳士どころではない。(He is far from being a gentleman. )<br/>Question: Is there is difference in these sentences between \"どころか\" and \"どころではない\" ?",
      "credits_raw": "フリザ",
      "content_sha256": "9f8b9907964ff05241d5bb2154e40f3ad61ef30c7ff486313e6fec2afca5a8e8",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "し・しまった・・・\n「Is there a difference」だよ。 タイプミス、許して下さい＞＜",
      "html": "し・しまった・・・<br/>「Is there a difference」だよ。 タイプミス、許して下さい＞＜",
      "credits_raw": "フリザ",
      "content_sha256": "818b8f55ffc989bbb1dee48f304e1a596fe69bc00de5471a7e92d0082da8629b",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "in notes it says about dokorodehanai at the end and dokorodehanaku in the middle, and by looking at the last example it would seem it's different to 'samui dewanai, kogoeshinu yo!', it's more like 'baai jya nai', so I was wondering if dokorodehanaku in the middle also means baaijanai?",
      "html": "in notes it says about dokorodehanai at the end and dokorodehanaku in the middle, and by looking at the last example it would seem it's different to 'samui dewanai, kogoeshinu yo!', it's more like 'baai jya nai', so I was wondering if dokorodehanaku in the middle also means baaijanai?",
      "credits_raw": "Snake",
      "content_sha256": "fa41633de92fbc184d8d1c98ba3a45536ae6667bc6e434c283c3e289899f2485",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "場合じゃない has a completely different context.The urgency of どころではない is not at all conveyed by 場合じゃない.\n場合 has a case, but どころではない has no case; you look everywhere and it's not there.",
      "html": "場合じゃない has a completely different context.The urgency of どころではない is not at all conveyed by 場合じゃない.<br/>場合 has a case, but どころではない has no case; you look everywhere and it's not there.",
      "credits_raw": "bamboo4",
      "content_sha256": "4b3965cec0e0b9ff441047298bb538fc3dce5c5275fed0ecaf4bc86cf5ec7e9b",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Er, what's with the usage instructions? They say dokorodehanai goes at the end, but in 3 examples it's in the middle of a sentence.",
      "html": "Er, what's with the usage instructions? They say dokorodehanai goes at the end, but in 3 examples it's in the middle of a sentence.",
      "credits_raw": "Quobobo",
      "content_sha256": "55717f76be6371357c246e8d1f8b9122a72d6ae699ca6a0a5d195693b33aa888",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "can we find any examples of dokoro de ha naku? that would seem more of a connective form, like nakute...",
      "html": "can we find any examples of dokoro de ha naku? that would seem more of a connective form, like nakute...",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "fb61c860dbd53ef8f7b1cc001fec0b52d6747125bb4e519bb0a60d4421399575",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "What about どころでは済まなくなる? Something like \"unforgivable\"?",
      "html": "What about どころでは済まなくなる? Something like \"unforgivable\"?",
      "credits_raw": "anna",
      "content_sha256": "2cd425d4b68281e313e54389d39bbaffb06c3bfcbe5eed7cee6004731986b710",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "this pattern means aru jyoutai ga atte nani nani ga dekinai.\nDoes this also having a meaning of \"far from\"?",
      "html": "this pattern means aru jyoutai ga atte nani nani ga dekinai.<br/>Does this also having a meaning of \"far from\"?",
      "credits_raw": "jayati",
      "content_sha256": "a7018ab656c13303bee2fcfabe77b751170de1185461f07287d6e28db67011e5",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Shouldn't #211 be \"dokoro de wa naku\" instead?",
      "html": "Shouldn't #211 be \"dokoro de wa naku\" instead?",
      "credits_raw": "MaDaZi",
      "content_sha256": "8a9f013801043df77638291730401caa4fc171723c3f1214f01d06e42791ddf4",
